  "description": "DINQAU crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group P 42/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C80 H76 Cl10 Co4 Gd4 N10 O26,0.5(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Co4 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Co5 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Co6 (Co) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 13 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.586-4.229 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.01-128.09°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [CoII4GdIII4(OH)4(chp)10(acac)6]·0.5MeCN. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies Co(II), Gd(III).",
